00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:12.690
even if nobody ever sees it.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:13.930
- And it's a little like Marie Kondo too,

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:14.920
you're letting it go.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.890
Like, thank you for the
experience, I'm done!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.100
- Yeah, totally!

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.780
And I'm terrified for this podcast

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.060
because I'm usually like the girl

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.670
twerking upside down on television,

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:24.178
and like falling down the stairs.

00:08:24.178 --> 00:08:25.090
(laughing)

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.040
That's me and everybody knows me!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.010
- There's room for all of it, Beth!

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:30.260
- But I realized is that
like, if I expect my guests

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.530
to come on and not talk about, you know,

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.700
not just the classic sort
of interview questions,

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.230
if I want them to get vulnerable
and honest, then I had to.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:40.070
And so I've revealed some stuff

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.130
and talked really deeply
about my mental health.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.560
But then hearing like that
other musicians that I admire

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.640
have panic attacks before
they go on stage, it's like-

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.130
- Oh my God, especially musicians, yeah.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.680
- Yes, let's talk through it.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.100
Brandy and I talked about when
she sang for Joni Mitchell

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.143
and how, you know-

00:08:54.143 --> 00:08:56.284
- I just started sweating
for her right now.

00:08:56.284 --> 00:08:57.718
- Did you really?
- Wow.

00:08:57.718 --> 00:09:00.390
- But if she can get through
that, I can get through.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.150
You know, there's something
about coming together

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:04.880
and speaking about mental health
openly, which for so long,

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.170
especially as women, we're
like, I can toughen up!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.130
You know, I can, I'm gonna
take care of my family,

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:10.580
I'm going to take care
of everybody around me.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.413
- It's all in that book.

00:09:11.413 --> 00:09:12.930
- "Untamed," cheetah!

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:13.763
- I know, I know.

00:09:13.763 --> 00:09:16.120
- So yeah, it's been amazingly
healing selfishly for me,

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.230
but also I hope it helps other people.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:20.490
- Yeah, I cannot wait to
be on it, first of all,

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.380
I would like to and also, I
can't wait to check it out.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.980
It sounds amazing.
- Thank you.

